**Problem Analysis**:
The `pygame.font.SysFont()` function expects a string (font name) as its first argument, but `None` is being passed. When `None` is passed, Pygame's internal font initialization code on Windows (`initsysfonts_win32()`) tries to process it as a font path/name, but it receives an integer instead of a string.

